{
  "about": "Resource-state keys (flyto-core 2.41.0). A host that reads establishes and occupies without importing Core must admit every 'admitted' contract and refuse every 'refused' one. Each fragment is merged into the base contract of its section; the normalized keys equal the fragment's. 'unchanged' pins the SHA-256 of the canonical JSON (sorted keys, no whitespace, UTF-8) of contracts that declare neither key, computed on 2.40.0: it must not move. 'overlaps' and 'satisfies' are the two rules a host applies to normalized contracts: whether two running calls on one resource conflict, and which required states a call still lacks after the states earlier completed calls established.",
